===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=noun|:inh|enm:fyr<id:fire>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|fyr}}, from {{inh|en|ang|fȳr|t=fire}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*fuir}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*fuïr}}, a regularised form of {{inh|en|gem-pro|*fōr|t=fire}}, ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*péh₂wr̥}}.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>  
{{col-top|2|cog}}
See also {{cog|sco|feier}}, {{m|sco|fyre|t=fire}}, {{cog|yol|vier}}, {{m|yol|vire|t=fire}}, {{cog|stq|Fjuur}}, {{m|stq|Fjúur|t=fire}}, {{cog|fy|fjoer|t=fire}}, {{cog|gsw|Füür|t=fire}}, {{cog|bar|Feia|t=fire}}, {{cog|gmw-cfr|Fauer}}, {{m|gmw-cfr|Feier}}, {{m|gmw-cfr|Füür|t=fire}}, {{cog|cim|bôar}}, {{m|cim|vaür}}, {{m|cim|vôar|t=fire}}, {{cog|nl|vier}}, {{m|nl|vuur|t=fire}}, {{cog|de|Feuer|t=fire}}, {{cog|nds-de|Füer}}, {{m|nds-de|Füür|t=fire}}, {{cog|lb|Feier|t=fire}}, {{cog|mhn|vaier|t=fire}}, {{cog|wym|faojer|t=fire}}, {{cog|vls|vier|t=fire}}, {{cog|yi|פֿײַער|t=fire}}, {{cog|da,nb,nn,sv|fyr|t=fire}}, {{cog|is|funi|t=fire}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐍉𐌽|t=fire}}. Also, compare {{cog|hy|հուր|t=fire}}, {{cog|el|πυρ|t=fire}}, {{cog|la|pūrgō|t=to clean, cleanse, clear, purge, purify}}, {{cog|xum|𐌐𐌉𐌓|t=fire}}, {{cog|bg|фир|t=ooze, pickle, soak}}, {{cog|pl|perz|t=smoke}}, {{cog|hit|𒉺𒄴𒄯|tr=paḫḫur|t=fire}}, {{cog|xlu|𒉺𒀀𒄷𒌋𒌨|tr=pāhūr|t=fire}}, {{w|Tocharian}} A/B {{m|xto|por}}/{{m|txb|puwar|t=fire}}. This was an inanimate noun whose animate counterpart was {{cog|ine-pro|*h₁n̥gʷnis}} (see ''[[ignite]]''). Cognate to {{m|en|pyre}}.
